  "inbound_message": "From: Marta Kowalczyk <marta.kowalczyk@mailbox.example>\nTo: Aerlink Customer Care <care@aerlink.example>\nDate: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 11:15:37 +0100\nSubject: AK808 3 August - crew shortage, compensation claim\n\nHello,\n\nBooking AER-9L5D2R. My flight AK808 from Edinburgh to Amsterdam on Monday 3rd\nAugust was cancelled at around six in the evening.\n\nThe woman at the gate told us directly that it was because the crew had not\nturned up. She said it twice and there were plenty of other passengers standing\nthere who heard her say it. I understand that a crew problem is the airline's own\nfault, which means this is not one of those situations where you can say it was\nout of your hands. So please process my compensation.\n\nI also had to stay in Edinburgh overnight because there was nothing else that\nevening and your desk had shut. I booked my own hotel and it cost me \u00a3112. I have\nthe receipt and I would like that back as well.\n\nMarta Kowalczyk\n",
  "decision": {
    "summary": "Marta Kowalczyk will receive a reimbursement of \u00a3112 for the hotel stay incurred due to the cancellation of her flight AK808 on 3rd August. The flight was cancelled due to extraordinary weather conditions, specifically freezing fog, which does not entitle her to any statutory compensation according to policy, as the cause falls under extraordinary circumstances.\n\nHere is the summary of actions taken:\n- Reviewed the booking and confirmed the details of the flight cancellation.\n- Found that, while duty of care is owed, no compensation is payable because the cancellation was due to extraordinary circumstances (weather-related).\n- Processed a goodwill reimbursement of \u00a3112 for the hotel expenses incurred, which matches the amount claimed.\n\nNo additional compensation is available under the circumstances, as specified by the entitlement assessment.",
    "escalated": false,
    "escalated_reason": null
  },
